To add a Gaussian filter before applying the Sobel operator, you can first create a Gaussian kernel with a standard deviation of your choice (e.g., `sigma` = 1 or 2) using the `fspecial()` function in MATLAB:

```matlab
sigma = 1; % Choose the standard deviation of the Gaussian filter
gaussian_kernel = fspecial('gaussian', [3 3], sigma);
```

Then, convolve the input image with the Gaussian kernel to apply the filter:

```matlab
filtered_image = conv2(input_image, gaussian_kernel, 'same');
```

After applying the Gaussian filter, you can proceed with the Sobel edge detection as described in your previous code:

```matlab
% Define Sobel operators in x and y directions
sobel_x = [-1 0 1; -2 0 2; -1 0 1];
sobel_y = [-1 -2 -1; 0 0 0; 1 2 1];

% Apply Sobel operator in x direction
edge_image_x = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_x, 'same');

% Apply Sobel operator in y direction
edge_image_y = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_y, 'same');

% Combine edges in both directions
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);

% Display edge image
imshow(edge_image);
```

By adding the Gaussian filter before the Sobel operator, you can help reduce the noise in the image and improve the accuracy of the edge detection results.

